From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: No geometry shaders on Arm's driver, and the GammaOS frontend's
 switches

The rest of what azahar-nano gets on GammaOS from outside these sources:

- vk_instance.h turns geometry shaders off under __ANDROID__ ("extremely
  expensive on tilers"); elsewhere it uses them when the driver has them,
  and Arm's Linux driver has. On the RG52 Mini the vertex and tiler work of
  a Super Mario 3D Land frame took 19.5 ms with them, 3.8 ms on GammaOS.
  Now they are off on Arm's driver too.
- GammaOS's frontend turns on vertex depth, render pass clears, folded
  clears, the hardware "keep inside" scissor and the JIT warm-up at every
  launch (azn_set_tweaks, azn_set_tweak); settings.h has them off, so the
  libretro core ran without them. Clears alone took 6.6 ms of a frame,
  0.7 ms with them.

With 006 and this, in Super Mario 3D Land 1-1 from the same save state, the
GPU's time per frame is that of GammaOS (slot0 14.4 / slot1 3.7 ms against
13.9 / 3.8 with both eyes) and the game runs at 60 frames a second with the
right eye off, 30 before.

--- a/src/citra_libretro/core_settings.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/core_settings.cpp
@@ -1016,6 +1016,17 @@
         LibRetro::FetchVariable(config::graphics::disable_right_eye_render, config::enabled) ==
         config::enabled;
 
+    // dArkOS: the switches GammaOS's frontend for azahar-nano turns on at every launch
+    // (azn_set_tweaks and azn_set_tweak): depth from the vertex stage so early depth testing
+    // stays on, clears done by render passes and folded into the next pass, the "keep inside"
+    // scissor by the hardware instead of a discard, and the JIT warm-up of the blocks compiled
+    // in the last run. They default to off in settings.h, so the libretro core had none.
+    Settings::values.gammaos_vertex_depth = true;
+    Settings::values.gammaos_renderpass_clears = true;
+    Settings::values.gammaos_fold_clears = true;
+    Settings::values.gammaos_hw_scissor = true;
+    Settings::values.gammaos_jit_warmup = true;
+
     Settings::values.use_disk_shader_cache =
         LibRetro::FetchVariable(config::graphics::use_disk_shader_cache, config::enabled) ==
         config::enabled;
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_instance.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_instance.h
@@ -124,7 +124,10 @@
         // cost even if it hurts accuracy somewhat. TODO: Make this an option
         return false;
 #else
-        return features.geometryShader;
+        // dArkOS: the Mali GPUs are tilers too. With geometry shaders on, Super Mario 3D Land
+        // spent 19.5 ms a frame on the RG52 Mini's vertex and tiler work, against 3.8 ms on
+        // GammaOS's Android build of the same code (Mali-G52 at 900 MHz, both eyes drawn).
+        return features.geometryShader && driver_id != vk::DriverIdKHR::eArmProprietary;
 #endif
     }
 
